## Spatial, temporal, and recurrence architecture

| Window | Front | Living middle | Rear / residue | Required transition |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | Polished rind, literal lemon, pepper, wet ginger | Citral, beta-pinene, Triplal micro-cut | First violet-metal and dry cedar glints | Citrus must reveal ginger, never replace it |
| 5–30 min | Ginger cortex contracts | Jessemal, dihydrojasmone, cis jasmone, terpinyl acetate expose warm fiber | Rose oxide, Leafovert, basil, Dynascone sharpen the cloth edge | Wet cut must become warm tissue rather than disappear |
| 30–120 min | Violet-green fiber | AIMI, ionones, Freesia, PEDMC, Mayol form tailored cloth | Cedar/vetiver grains become legible through air gaps | Floral volume must read as fabric around ginger, not a bouquet |
| 2–6 h | Dry violet-root and cedar pencil line | Tonka absolute, coumarin, Sandalore, Polysantol yield inward | Vetiver, Koavone, Cashmeran, Romandolide hold contour | Hard/soft opposition must remain connected by shared woody-fibrous edges |
| 6–24 h | Faint dry cut | Hayed tonka and sandal warmth | Cedar-vetiver residue inside one clean woody aura | Late material must recall ginger's fiber and warmth without false persistence |

All temporal language is intended architecture. It is `NOT OBSERVED`.

### Explicit transition links and textural roles

| Link | Shared edge | Failure if absent |
|---|---|---|
| Peel -> ginger cortex | citral, linalyl acetate, pepper, beta-pinene | citrus cleaner beside unrelated ginger |
| Cortex -> rhizome heart | Ginger EO, Jessemal, dihydrojasmone, cis jasmone | ginger top falls into a hollow heart |
| Rhizome -> violet cloth | cis jasmone, ethyl linalool, AIMI, ionones | floral powder appears as a separate object |
| Violet cloth -> green incision | Leafovert, basil, rose oxide, Dynascone, Scentenal | cloth lacks leaf realism and perimeter |
| Green incision -> air | Cyclamen, Floralozone, Helional, Hedione HC | green becomes harsh, flat, or marine |
| Violet cloth -> cedar grain | Allyl Ionone, Dihydro Beta Ionone, Cashmeran, Iso E | abrupt cosmetic-to-wood splice |
| Ginger fiber -> vetiver root | terpinyl acetate, clary, Koavone, Vetival | base loses the named subject |
| Cedar grain -> yielding sandal | Koavone, Sandalore, Polysantol | woods become a rigid stacked wall |
| Vetiver root -> tonka grain | Coumarin, Tonkarome, Tonka Absolute | tonka reads edible or pasted on |
| Base interior -> aura | Polysantol, Cashmeran, Romandolide | musk floats as detergent outside the perfume |

The intended textures are polished, waxed, wet-cut, crisp, fatty, fibrous, tailored-cloth, leafy, metallic, bitter, humid, mineral, pencil-dry, rooty, hayed, creamy-yielding, textile, slow, and clean-woody. Count is a conservation floor only; physical smelling must determine whether these roles are actually distinct and connected.

