## Controlled blinded acceptance protocol

### Primary successor comparison

- Compare immutable V4 control against V5 at constant 6,000 uL concentrate and identical 20% finished concentration.
- Prepare two independent master sets on different occasions; from each master, make duplicate coded pours. Use anonymous random codes, balanced presentation order, equal application mass, identical substrate, and a sealed code key.
- Read free description before scores at 0, 5, 30, and 120 minutes, then 6 and 24 hours.
- Score 0–10: L'Homme identity; ginger cortex; warm ginger interior; ginger-to-violet continuity; violet-leaf realism; violet-to-cedar continuity; literal cedar/vetiver grain; tonka-sandal richness; airy/dense simultaneity; spatial depth; texture differentiation; late ginger recurrence; overall liking; luxury/style.
- Score defects separately: citrus cleaner takeover; marine/blue drift; rose recognition; lipstick iris; woody-amber wall; muddiness; metallic glare; sweetness/gourmand drift; musk detergent effect; fatigue.

Acceptance requires L'Homme identity at least 6/10 and no more than a one-point drop versus V4; overall liking not lower; transitions and spatiality not lower; at least two target depth/texture axes improve by at least one point; no drift defect worsens by more than one point; both independent master sets show the same direction. If perceived intensity differs by more than one point, intensity-match and repeat. Discordant masters are `HOLD`, not averaged into success.

### Highest-value causal follow-ups only

1. **TRACE-RELIEF omission:** replace Beta-Pinene 1% 10 + Rose Oxide 1% 10 + Triplal 0.1% 10 + Floralozone 10% 20 with 50 uL DPG. This tests whether the controlled incisions add 3D relief or merely harshness/marine glare.
2. **NATURAL-TONKA texture:** replace Tonka Absolute 10% 450 one-for-one with DPG while keeping Tonkarome unchanged. This tests whether the natural grain is perceptible and improves the yielding chamber. A null result means the hypothesis is non-informative at this dose; it does not validate more material.
3. **VIOLET-TISSUE omission:** replace Dihydro Beta Ionone 150 + Freesia HDI 80 + Cis Jasmone 30 with 260 uL DPG. This tests whether the new tissue connects ginger, violet, and cedar or adds cosmetic blur.

Do not run all follow-ups blindly. Run only the arm implicated by the primary free descriptions and defect scores.

## Claim ceiling

This artifact is a target-first theory formula and controlled experimental design. It has not been physically compounded or smelled. Passing local parsers, donor-independence checks, OAV calculations, or release gates cannot establish similarity, liking, hedonism, luxury, completion, complexity, depth, three-dimensionality, safety, stability, diffusion, longevity, maturation, or commercial release.

